#: NAVIGATION.md:1 NAVIGATION.md:41
msgid "Path integral metadynamics"
msgstr "Path Integral Metadynamics"

#: NAVIGATION.md:3
msgid ""
"Path integrals simulatins are able to describe the quantum thermodynamics of"
" distinguishable particles at finite temperature, and are the most accurate "
"approach to describe the behavior of light nuclei (e.g. hydrogen) at room "
"temperature and above."
msgstr ""
"Path Integral シミュレーションは、有限温度における Distinguishable Particles の Quantum "
"Thermodynamics を記述でき、室温以上での軽い原子核（水素など）の振る舞いを記述する最も精密な手法である。"

#: NAVIGATION.md:8
msgid ""
"They can be combined with metadynamics to accelerate the sampling of rare "
"events, and compute a \"quantum free energies\" that reflect (in an "
"approximate way) the effect of zero-point energy and tunneling on reaction "
"rates."
msgstr ""
"Metadynamics と組み合わせることで Rare Events の Sampling を加速し、Zero-point Energy と "
"Tunneling が Reaction Rates に及ぼす影響を近似的に反映した「量子的な自由エネルギー」を計算できる。"

#: NAVIGATION.md:12
msgid "Free-energy of the Zundel cation"
msgstr "Zundel Cation の自由エネルギー"

#: NAVIGATION.md:14
msgid ""
"This lecture provide a hands-on interactive tutorial (that you can also "
"download and run locally) that uses the [i-PI code](http://ipi-code.org) to "
"perform path-integral simulations for the Zundel cation, a protonated water "
"dimer. PLUMED is used to compute appropriate collective variables, using an "
"input as follows"
msgstr ""
"この講義は、[i-PI code](http://ipi-code.org) を用いて Zundel Cation（Protonated Water "
"Dimer）の Path Integral シミュレーションを行う、対話型の実習チュートリアルである。ダウンロードして手元でも実行できる。PLUMED "
"は、次のような入力を使って適切な Collective Variables を計算するために用いる。"

#: NAVIGATION.md:33
msgid ""
"Depending on your previous experience, you may want to follow the lessons on"
" metadynamics, and the external tutorial on path integral simulations."
msgstr ""
"これまでの経験に応じて、Metadynamics のレッスンや Path Integral シミュレーションの外部チュートリアルを先に学ぶとよい。"

